WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:21.756
"Aunt Jo," Daisy cried, dashing into Jo's study, "the boys won't let me play football!

2
00:00:22.996 --> 00:00:25.237
They say girls can't play football."

3
00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:28.919
"That's ridiculous!"

4
00:00:29.339 --> 00:00:31.340
Jo retorted, putting down her pen.

5
00:00:32.972 --> 00:00:36.033
"I know girls can play because I did it when I was young."

6
00:00:37.994 --> 00:00:38.975
Daisy sighed.

7
00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:44.117
"I'm tired of doing things by myself—will you play with me?"

8
00:00:44.137 --> 00:00:49.319
"I will later, but right now I'm getting ready to go into town.

9
00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.441
Come with me, and if you want, you can stay with your mother for a few days."

10
00:00:54.461 --> 00:00:59.924
"I'd like to see Mama and baby Josy, but I don't want to stay with them.

11
00:01:01.292 --> 00:01:03.733
Demi would miss me, and I love being here!"

12
00:01:03.753 --> 00:01:09.136
"All right, but how will you entertain yourself until I'm ready?"

13
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:15.200
Daisy shrugged and said, "Can you make up a new game or activity for me?"

14
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:20.342
"Hmm, it'll take a while to think up something brand-new.

15
00:01:21.783 --> 00:01:24.124
Why don't you see what Asia is preparing for lunch?"

16
00:01:24.144 --> 00:01:26.726
"That's a good idea!"

17
00:01:27.306 --> 00:01:30.708
Daisy cried, running off to visit the cook in her kitchen.

18
00:01:32.244 --> 00:01:36.346
In five minutes Daisy returned with a spot of flour on her nose.

19
00:01:36.366 --> 00:01:40.448
"Please, Aunt Jo, may I make cookies with Asia?"

20
00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:41.468
she asked.

21
00:01:41.488 --> 00:01:45.550
"I won't bother her, and it would be such fun!"

22
00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:53.093
"Go ahead, and stay as long as you like," Jo said, relieved that Daisy had found something to

23
00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:58.996
do. And suddenly Jo knew how to keep her niece entertained.

24
00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.523
That afternoon Daisy visited her mother, Meg, while Jo went shopping.

25
00:02:10.266 --> 00:02:16.870
Jo returned later with many mysterious parcels, but all she said was "They're for Daisy."

26
00:02:19.511 --> 00:02:23.014
When it was time to leave, Meg tied Daisy's bonnet.

27
00:02:24.655 --> 00:02:27.864
"Be a good girl for Aunt Jo.

28
00:02:27.884 --> 00:02:32.448
She's very kind to think of this for you because she doesn't like this activity much herself."

29
00:02:36.131 --> 00:02:41.815
At this, the two sisters burst out laughing, which only increased Daisy's curiosity.

30
00:02:45.458 --> 00:02:48.781
All the way home, Daisy pestered Jo with questions.

31
00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:52.204
"Have I ever seen this game before?"

32
00:02:52.224 --> 00:02:57.388
"You've never seen one as nice as this," Jo replied.

33
00:02:59.372 --> 00:03:02.414
Daisy heard something rattling in the back of the carriage.

34
00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:05.236
"Is it for the boys too?"

35
00:03:05.616 --> 00:03:06.217
she asked.

36
00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:12.081
"No, it's just for you and me and Bess," Jo said.

37
00:03:13.362 --> 00:03:16.544
Bess was Daisy's cousin, Laurie and Amy's daughter.

38
00:03:16.564 --> 00:03:22.188
"I ran into Uncle Laurie in town, and he helped me choose the different parts."

39
00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:28.212
"Oh, the game must be wonderful because Uncle Laurie buys the best presents!"

40
00:03:28.512 --> 00:03:29.292
Daisy said.

41
00:03:30.853 --> 00:03:35.235
By the time they reached home, Daisy was nearly wild with anticipation.

42
00:03:36.596 --> 00:03:42.438
But Jo said Daisy couldn't do the new activity until she finished her lessons the next day.

43
00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:50.922
Daisy's excitement soon spread to the boys, who offered to help Jo set up Daisy's present.

44
00:03:50.942 --> 00:03:59.650
"Sorry, no boys allowed," Jo said, treating the four boys exactly as they'd treated Daisy.

45
00:04:01.451 --> 00:04:05.773
At this, the boys meekly went away and sought out Daisy.

46
00:04:07.494 --> 00:04:14.717
They offered to play football, marbles, or anything she liked, but Daisy only shook her head and smiled,

47
00:04:15.137 --> 00:04:17.018
delighted to turn them down.

48
00:04:19.179 --> 00:04:22.240
The next morning Daisy quickly finished her lessons.

49
00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.702
Jo took her up to the playroom, where Daisy heard something bubbling.

50
00:04:36.265 --> 00:04:37.786
a real little kitchen!"

51
00:04:38.206 --> 00:04:39.066
Daisy cried.

52
00:04:40.287 --> 00:04:43.948
She ran over to the stove and saw a boiling tea kettle.

53
00:04:45.249 --> 00:04:52.012
On either side of the stove were shelves filled with measuring cups, mixing bowls, and pots and pans.

54
00:04:55.036 --> 00:04:57.677
Cabinets held spices and other ingredients.

55
00:04:59.637 --> 00:05:05.939
"You had so much fun making cookies that I decided you needed a kitchen of your own," Jo

56
00:05:05.999 --> 00:05:11.701
explained. "Why don't you pretend you're a cook now, and go to market."

57
00:05:13.101 --> 00:05:14.442
Daisy looked perplexed.

58
00:05:14.462 --> 00:05:16.802
"But where's the market?"

59
00:05:17.102 --> 00:05:17.683
she asked.

60
00:05:17.703 --> 00:05:20.983
"In Asia's kitchen, of course!"

61
00:05:24.416 --> 00:05:31.281
Daisy went downstairs and returned with a potato, some squash, and the ingredients for a small pie.

62
00:05:32.261 --> 00:05:36.324
With Jo's help, she quickly made the pie and put it in the oven.

63
00:05:37.865 --> 00:05:41.348
Next she boiled the potato and steamed the squash.

64
00:05:42.869 --> 00:05:49.133
After setting the table, she admired the contents of her kitchen as well as her new apron and

65
00:05:49.193 --> 00:05:55.689
cap. But when she checked on her pie, she saw that disaster had struck!

66
00:05:55.709 --> 00:05:58.269
"Aunt Jo!

67
00:05:58.849 --> 00:06:00.310
The pie burned!"

68
00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.811
Tears rolled down Daisy's face.

69
00:06:03.831 --> 00:06:06.331
"Oh no!"

70
00:06:06.912 --> 00:06:10.372
Jo cried, putting down the book she was reading to Teddy.

71
00:06:10.392 --> 00:06:13.953
"I should have paid more attention!"

72
00:06:15.694 --> 00:06:19.875
Using a potholder, she removed the blackened pastry from the oven.

73
00:06:19.895 --> 00:06:27.423
"When we were shopping for your kitchen, Uncle Laurie took great delight in reminding me of my cooking

74
00:06:27.463 --> 00:06:34.147
disasters. This pie isn't fit to eat, but I'm sure your dolls will enjoy the rest of the

75
00:06:34.207 --> 00:06:42.293
meal." No sooner had Daisy settled her dolls at the table than the boys swarmed into the room.

76
00:06:42.313 --> 00:06:44.655
"What are you cooking?"

77
00:06:44.935 --> 00:06:45.715
Demi asked.

78
00:06:45.735 --> 00:06:48.237
"It smells delicious!"

79
00:06:48.657 --> 00:06:50.439
Nat added, rubbing his belly.

80
00:06:50.459 --> 00:06:56.174
"Hey, that steamer looks like something we could use," Tommy said to Jack.

81
00:06:57.255 --> 00:07:03.418
Daisy looked alarmed when Jack nodded in agreement and said, "That heavy pot would be perfect for melting

82
00:07:03.458 --> 00:07:05.860
down—" "Aha!"

83
00:07:07.221 --> 00:07:08.421
Just then Mr.

84
00:07:08.521 --> 00:07:09.482
Bauer arrived.

85
00:07:09.502 --> 00:07:12.464
"So this is your new kitchen, Daisy.

86
00:07:12.484 --> 00:07:15.586
I hope you're a better cook than Aunt Jo!"

87
00:07:15.606 --> 00:07:19.428
"All right, Fritz, that's enough!"

88
00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.222
Jo said, clapping her hands and frowning at her husband.

89
00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:27.885
"Everyone out of the kitchen except Daisy!"

90
00:07:27.905 --> 00:07:32.587
"But we haven't told Daisy what we want her to make for us!"

91
00:07:32.928 --> 00:07:34.108
Tommy protested.

92
00:07:34.128 --> 00:07:40.312
"What about my favorite German dish—cabbage soup with herring and cherries?"

93
00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:42.193
Mr. Bauer suggested.

94
00:07:42.213 --> 00:07:45.395
"I can't even make that!"

95
00:07:45.795 --> 00:07:47.576
Jo said, shaking her head.

96
00:07:48.972 --> 00:07:52.035
But Daisy was ready for another cooking challenge.

97
00:07:52.055 --> 00:07:54.938
"I'll give it a try, Uncle Fritz!"

98
00:07:55.419 --> 00:07:56.420
she said happily.
